<item>
            <title>[LU-20887] LFU: Object Stream of an in-service OST does not carry the owner FID</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20887</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Problem&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An OST object records the MDT file it belongs to: the parent FID in the object&apos;s &lt;tt&gt;trusted.fid&lt;/tt&gt;, or in the LMA on OSTs with 256-byte inodes (&lt;tt&gt;LMAC_STRIPE_INFO&lt;/tt&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LFU already reports it when it reads a target directly. For a stopped OST, &lt;tt&gt;llapi_scan_device()&lt;/tt&gt; answers &lt;tt&gt;LLAPI_SCAN_OWNER&lt;/tt&gt; / &lt;tt&gt;lfsr_owner_fid&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20606&quot; title=&quot;LFU: implement ldiskfs device scanner&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20606&quot;&gt;LU-20606&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20637&quot; title=&quot;LFU: Output Format module to generate pathnames from FIDs&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20637&quot;&gt;LU-20637&lt;/a&gt;), and &lt;tt&gt;--fid2path&lt;/tt&gt; names each object by its file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For an OST that is mounted and serving, the scan goes through the Object Stream from the OSD otable iterator (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20720&quot; title=&quot;LFU: in-kernel OSD scanner&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20720&quot;&gt;LU-20720&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20722&quot; title=&quot;LFU: lfind on a live target via the in-kernel OSD scanner&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20722&quot;&gt;LU-20722&lt;/a&gt;). Its record, &lt;tt&gt;struct lfu_rec&lt;/tt&gt;, carries the attributes, &lt;tt&gt;trusted.lma&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;trusted.som&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;trusted.link&lt;/tt&gt; and the presence of LOV/LMV, but not &lt;tt&gt;trusted.fid&lt;/tt&gt;. So a scan of an in-service OST lists objects but cannot say which files they belong to.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Whyitmatters&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Why it matters&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the scan an OST drain needs: the OST stays mounted while its files are migrated away, and the list of files with objects on it should come from that one OST instead of a scan of every MDT. The same applies to shrinking an OST and to a parallel data mover that consumes the LFU stream.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reading the mounted device from outside is not an alternative, because it gives stale results. In a test, a scan of the raw disk of a mounted ldiskfs OST named none of the newly written files, and debugfs on a live OST found 441 of 1073 files.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Proposedfix&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Proposed fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A patch on top of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20720&quot; title=&quot;LFU: in-kernel OSD scanner&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20720&quot;&gt;LU-20720&lt;/a&gt; / &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20722&quot; title=&quot;LFU: lfind on a live target via the in-kernel OSD scanner&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20722&quot;&gt;LU-20722&lt;/a&gt; / &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20730&quot; title=&quot;LFU: llapi_scan_mount() to scan a filesystem&apos;s MDTs from a client&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20730&quot;&gt;LU-20730&lt;/a&gt; series:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;dt_otable_lfu_rec()&lt;/tt&gt; reads the parent FID through &lt;tt&gt;DORA_XATTR&lt;/tt&gt;, from &lt;tt&gt;trusted.fid&lt;/tt&gt; or from the LMA, only for OST objects (and objects with no LMA), so MDT scans do not pay for it.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The FID is carried in the record&apos;s tail after the link, as &lt;tt&gt;struct lfu_owner&lt;/tt&gt;, flagged by a new &lt;tt&gt;LFU_REC_HAVE_OWNER&lt;/tt&gt; bit. The header size and &lt;tt&gt;LFU_WIRE_VERSION&lt;/tt&gt; do not change, so older readers skip it and the client &lt;tt&gt;OBD_IDX_READ&lt;/tt&gt; stream stays compatible.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Userspace hands it to the scanner as the head of a &lt;tt&gt;trusted.fid&lt;/tt&gt;, so &lt;tt&gt;LLAPI_SCAN_OWNER&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;--fid2path&lt;/tt&gt; work on a mounted OST as on a stopped one.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;New conf-sanity test_305.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Tested on el9 (kernel 5.14, ldiskfs): test_305 passes with the patch (20 written files named by owner, never-written objects not named) and fails with the kernel-side change reverted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Openpoints&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Open points&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Objects that were created but never written or setattr&apos;ed have no parent FID on the OST, so they are still reported without an owner. For a drain they need either the parent FID written at create time or a layout-only check on the MDT.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Not tested: ZFS OSTs, OSTs with 256-byte inodes (the LMA path), the client &lt;tt&gt;OBD_IDX_READ&lt;/tt&gt; stream.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Passing the raw disk of a target that is mounted through a mapped device (for example dm-flakey) silently falls back to reading the live disk from outside. The scan should refuse or warn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
